# Derived data. Rebuildable at any time with `python3 store.py data`.
# This is a binary that changes every day, so committing it would make git
# store a fresh 60MB+ copy daily and balloon the repo into gigabytes.
data/index.sqlite
data/index.sqlite-wal
data/index.sqlite-shm

# Python noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# NOTE: data/objects/ and data/snapshots/ are deliberately NOT ignored.
# Those two directories ARE the dataset. Committing every snapshot is the
# point: the git history is the timestamped, third-party witnessed record of
# what the registry served on each date, which is what lets someone else trust
# your "before" when you report a mutation.